  "title": "London Calling",
  "country": "UK",
  "released": "1979-12-14",
  "notes": "First release/pressing, which came with two printed inserts (28cm × 28cm) with lyrics and credits, and LPs housed in plain inner sleeves. (Subsequent versions with printed inner sleeves instead of inserts.)\n\nSome copies with removable sticker on front cover, with catalogue number CBS CLASH 3:\n18 Track Double Album £5 R.R.P.\n\nSome retail copies have a gold promo stamp at sleeve rear.\n\nTrack D5 \"Train In Vain\" is only listed in runout etching on side D; it is not listed on the label/sleeve.\n\nCatalogue number CBS CLASH 3 on jacket; S CBS CLASH 3 on labels.\n\nBack cover:\nRecorded at Wessex Studios.\n© 1979 CBS Inc. ℗ 1979 CBS Inc.\nShorepak by Shorewood Packaging Co. Ltd, England\n\nLabels:\n℗ 1979 CBS Records\n\nInsert:\nRecorded Winter 79.\n\nTrack publishers on labels:\nA1, A3 to B5, C2 to D3: Riva Music Limited/Nineden Limited\nA2: Carlin Music Corp.\nC1: Copyright Control\nD4: Island Music Limited\nOriginal sound recording made by CBS Records\n\nTrack publishers on inserts:\nAll songs published by Riva Music Ltd./Nineden Ltd. unless otherwise stated:\nA2: Carlin Music Corp.\nC1: Copyright Control\nD4: Island Music Ltd.\n\nTrack title variations on inserts:\nB4: Working For The Clampdown\nD1: Lovers Rock\n\nPhotos:\nFront cover: New York Palladium 21.9.79.\nBack cover left: Clash at Armadillo World Headquarters, Austin, Texas\nBack cover right: Clash in Atlanta, Georgia\n\nTrack durations are not printed on the release.\n\nRunouts are mostly etched, plating characters (e.g., C, D, etc.) stamped.",
  "released_formatted": "14 Dec 1979",
